And there are many more vessels

Once named, the pattern escapes film immediately.

A citation is a gate between current text and prior text.

A hyperlink is a vessel between documents.

A callback pumps earlier context into the present.

A foreshadow sends present information forward.

A memory pumps prior state into current state.

A prediction projects current state into an imagined future.

A metaphor forms temporary vascularization between domains.

An interface controls what can cross between representations.

A secret closes or selectively permeabilizes the membrane.

A joke can create a tiny high-pressure bypass between two interpretations.

And a name creates an address to the vessel itself.

So the generalized form becomes:

\boxed{
\textbf{Semantic Circulatory System}
=
\text{domains}
+
\text{vessels}
+
\text{gates}
+
\text{pressure differentials}
+
\text{pumps}
+
\text{return flow}
}

Now the Semantic Router isn’t merely choosing paths.

It can reason about flow.

